{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_d78a3c71-9284-4a5b-a226-61a85f79fe31","role":"user","created":1795129664,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c1de46c46bd9494","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"resultType":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","text":"===== PAGE 3 =====\nDorionis Metrology\nDocument ref. DM-RI-2025-7410  Revision B\nPrinted on 06/10/2025\nPage 3/5\n2. Measurements\nTable 1 - Readings\nParameter\nAs found\nAs left\nMean\nas left\nTolerance\nE1\nE2\nE3\nE1\nE2\nE3\nDose volume\n1,010\n1,000\n930\n960\n980\n910\n950\n± 80 µL\nFlow rate\n19.38\n—\n—\n—\nOperating pressure\n127.63\n152.29\n—\n—\nTemperature\n24.5\n26.0\n—\n—\nReadings table units: doses in µL, flow in L/h, pressure in psi, temperature in °C.\nTable 2 - Ratings\nRating\nValue\nModel range (OEM)\n1 – 20 mL\nTank capacity\n60 L\nLine volume\n231 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 20 µL\nMax. flow\n37.2 L/h\nMax. allowable pressure\n24.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n16.6 bar\nReplacements\nThe customer was briefed on the points of attention noted during the visit. No replacement was needed; part UL-958-R (head\ngasket) was nevertheless ordered as a precaution. Part UL-373-K (diaphragm) was inspected and found in good condition.\nCleaning-in-place instructions were reminded to the production team.\nField team\nChecks were carried out with calibrated instruments; certificates are available to the customer. Access to the machine was granted\nafter electrical and pneumatic lock-out by the line manager. Grace Marsh led the visit with the support of James Ainsley, at the\nrequest of Declan Kerrigan.\n\n\n\n===== PAGE 4 =====","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"===== PAGE 3 =====\nDorionis Metrology\nDocument ref. DM-RI-2025-7410  Revision B\nPrinted on 06/10/2025\nPage 3/5\n2. Measurements\nTable 1 - Readings\nParameter\nAs found\nAs left\nMean\nas left\nTolerance\nE1\nE2\nE3\nE1\nE2\nE3\nDose volume\n1,010\n1,000\n930\n960\n980\n910\n950\n± 80 µL\nFlow rate\n19.38\n—\n—\n—\nOperating pressure\n127.63\n152.29\n—\n—\nTemperature\n24.5\n26.0\n—\n—\nReadings table units: doses in µL, flow in L/h, pressure in psi, temperature in °C.\nTable 2 - Ratings\nRating\nValue\nModel range (OEM)\n1 – 20 mL\nTank capacity\n60 L\nLine volume\n231 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 20 µL\nMax. flow\n37.2 L/h\nMax. allowable pressure\n24.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n16.6 bar\nReplacements\nThe customer was briefed on the points of attention noted during the visit. No replacement was needed; part UL-958-R (head\ngasket) was nevertheless ordered as a precaution. Part UL-373-K (diaphragm) was inspected and found in good condition.\nCleaning-in-place instructions were reminded to the production team.\nField team\nChecks were carried out with calibrated instruments; certificates are available to the customer. Access to the machine was granted\nafter electrical and pneumatic lock-out by the line manager. Grace Marsh led the visit with the support of James Ainsley, at the\nrequest of Declan Kerrigan.\n\n\n\n===== PAGE 4 =====","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
