{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1795129684-5IgQnIk8oJI30jblHdR9","role":"assistant","created":1795129690,"content":[{"type":"toolRequest","id":"chatcmpl-tool-849d3e783c77ebe9","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cd /travail && grep -n -i -E \"nevvex|constructeur|manufacturer|ateliers|logo\" work/textes/doc-034.txt; echo ---; sed -n '80,180p' work/textes/doc-034.txt; echo \"=== 035/040 tech\"; grep -n -i -E \"tech|respons|lead|particip|demand\" work/textes/doc-035.txt work/textes/doc-040.txt | head -30"}}},"_meta":{"goose.toolCall.providerIndex":0,"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true,"inference":{"provider":"openai","requestedModel":"deepseek-v4.1-flash"},"operations":{"llm":{"advertised_tools":["analyze","apps__create_app","apps__delete_app","apps__iterate_app","apps__list_apps","delegate","edit","extensionmanager__list_resources","extensionmanager__manage_extensions","extensionmanager__read_resource","extensionmanager__search_available_extensions","load","load_skill","read_image","shell","tree","write"]}}}}}
{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_c277d6d0-5c59-4ea3-9061-285c9242e102","role":"user","created":1795129690,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"chatcmpl-tool-849d3e783c77ebe9","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"resultType":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","text":"24:Manufacturer :\n91:N | NEVVEX\n142:The manufacturer's documentation was available on site and up to date. The report was reviewed on 21 August 2025. Guards\n---\nsettled at 5'100 µL on average, against 4'650 µL on arrival. Guide lubrication was topped up as per the manual.\nReplacements\nThe prevention plan was reviewed with the site safety department before work started. Part NE-785-D (check valve) was\ninspected and found in good condition.\nDiagram\n\n\n[IMAGE p1 #1 bbox=(437,59,557,98) texte OCR:]\nNEVEVEX | NC | Calibration Ltd\n\n[IMAGE p1 #2 bbox=(415,144,510,175) texte OCR:]\nN | NEVVEX\n\n\n===== PAGE 2 =====\nNEVEVEX CALIBRATION LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. NC-RI-2025-5530\nPrinted on 24/08/2025\n2 / 3\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nreference pressure\ngauge\nRiliovane\nIN-75438\n19/04/2025\nreference flow meter\nNerorrix\nIN-49198\n31/03/2025\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nNE-146-R\ndosing nozzle\nreplaced\n156.62 €\nNE-785-D\ncheck valve\ninspected, kept\n248.02 €\nNE-508-K\npiston seal\nordered (not fitted)\n433.72 €\nNE-765-R\nreturn spring\nquoted\n459.71 €\nField team\nThe production manager was kept informed at each step of the visit. James Mahon took part in the visit, at the request of Olivia\nKerrigan.\nTechnician's opinion\nProducts dosed on this line are aqueous and of low viscosity; no hazardous product was in the circuit during the visit. At the end of\nthe tests, the equipment must not return to production as it stands.\nApproval workflow\nThe manufacturer's documentation was available on site and up to date. The report was reviewed on 21 August 2025. Guards\nwere refitted and their interlocks checked before restart.\nNotes\nNote, equipment: Corvex 160.\nFor the record, date of intervention: 15 August 2025.\nNote, lead technician: Erin Pryce.\nThe upstream conveyor Corvex C49 (flow 1.31 L/min, pressure 6.0 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network\nruns at 6.0 bar.\nReport prepared by James Mahon.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\n\n\n[IMAGE p2 #1 bbox=(40,56,462,311) texte OCR:]\nTank | Piston unit | Line: 826 mL | 2 | Capacity: 20 L\n\n[IMAGE p2 #2 bbox=(34,335,209,403) texte OCR:]\nOSTIOVANMOTOR | TYPEM92-2P | N°M6634037 | 2.2kW | 2890min-1 | 230/400V | 50Hz | IP55\n\n\n===== PAGE 3 =====\nNEVEVEX CALIBRATION LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. NC-RI-2025-5530\nPrinted on 24/08/2025\n3 / 3\nNext preventive visit: 13/02/2026.\nTechnician:\nCustomer approval: Megan Doyle\nValidation date : 23/08/2025\n\n\n[IMAGE p3 #1 bbox=(40,89,150,123) texte OCR:]\nK\n\n[IMAGE p3 #2 bbox=(304,101,414,135) texte OCR:]\n>> | n | M=== 035/040 tech\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:4:ORYENIS TECHNIQUES  |  RAPPORT D INTERVENTION\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:28:Date de la demande :\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:36:Les traces de produit séché sur le bâti ont été nettoyées. La demande d'intervention a été reçue le 30 juillet 2025. Le siège du\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:79:Demande d'intervention\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:96:ORYENIS | Techniques\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:103:ORYENIS TECHNIQUES  |  RAPPORT D INTERVENTION\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:139:Les filtres d'aspiration ont été démontés, rincés et remis en place. Yann Barbier a participé à l'intervention, à la demande de\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:141:Avis du technicien\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:164:ORYENIS TECHNIQUES  |  RAPPORT D INTERVENTION\nwork/textes/doc-035.txt:168:Le technicien :\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:4:ORYENIS TECHNIQUES  |  RAPPORT D INTERVENTION\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:30:Date de la demande :\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:41:une demande du 30 décembre 2025. Le siège du client se trouve à Lamballe. Aucune fuite n'a été constatée sur les raccords\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:105:ORYENIS | Techniques\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:109:ORYENIS TECHNIQUES  |  RAPPORT D INTERVENTION\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:115:en bon état. Le responsable de production a été informé du déroulement de l'intervention à chaque étape.\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:153:Le poste de travail a été laissé propre et dégagé à la fin de la visite. Élodie Perrin a participé à l'intervention, à la demande de\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:155:Avis du technicien\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:160:L'accès à la machine a été rendu possible après consignation électrique et pneumatique par le responsable de ligne. Le rapport a\nwork/textes/doc-040.txt:177:ORYENISTECHNIQUES|RAPPORTDINTERVENTION | Ref.OT-RI-2026-8069 | Anoter, statut:A revoir. | Erratum:dansle tableau des mesures,lire3500ml/min au lieu de3030ml/minpour debit. | Le convoyeur amontNeveltikC15(debit6450mlmin,pression5,8bar)n'estpasconcerneparcetteintervention;lereseau dair | deatelieresta7,0bar. | A l'arrivee,'equipement etait jugenonconforme. | Prochainevisitepreventive:08.07.26. | Letechnicien: | Approbationclient:ManonDelmas | Datedevalidation:18.01.26 | Imprimele28.01.26 | 3/3","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"24:Manufacturer :\n91:N | NEVVEX\n142:The manufacturer's documentation was available on site and up to date. The report was reviewed on 21 August 2025. Guards\n---\nsettled at 5'100 µL on average, against 4'650 µL on arrival. Guide lubrication was topped up as per the manual.\nReplacements\nThe prevention plan was reviewed with the site safety department before work started. Part NE-785-D (check valve) was\ninspected and found in good condition.\nDiagram\n\n\n[IMAGE p1 #1 bbox=(437,59,557,98) texte OCR:]\nNEVEVEX | NC | Calibration Ltd\n\n[IMAGE p1 #2 bbox=(415,144,510,175) texte OCR:]\nN | NEVVEX\n\n\n===== PAGE 2 =====\nNEVEVEX CALIBRATION LTD 