{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_1e263493-5d27-4878-b6f8-635be6088bbf","role":"user","created":1795129872,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"chatcmpl-tool-96ad83f89d2dbfdc","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"resultType":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","text":"##########doc-004\n||===== PAGE 1 =====|VEXITIK SERVICES LTD|Printed on 28 Mar 2026|sheet 1/4|Report VS-RI-2026-6396|TECHNICAL INTERVENTION REPORT|Report reference : VS-RI-2026-6396|Supersedes : VS-RI-2026-6021|PO number : PO-879116|Job no. : AFF-86877|Customer : Mirlor Foods, Head office: Telford|Installation : Line 1, rotary filling machine|Equipment : Ulvorgen 600|Manufacturer :|Serial number : FE836339|Asset no. : INV-98493|Request date : 10 Mar 2026|Issue date : 23 Mar 2026|Date of intervention : 22 Mar 2026|The customer was briefed on the points of attention noted during the visit. Operators reported short stoppages at shift start, with no|alarm message. Demineralised water at room temperature was used for all tests.|I. BACKGROUND|Background and equipment|Guide lubrication was topped up as per the manual. Suction filters were removed, rinsed and refitted. The visit concerns the dosing|equipment of line 1. It is driven by a Vergen motor, type T91-4P. Checks were carried out with calibrated instruments; certificates|are available to the customer. The night shift was informed of the adjustments made.|Course of the visit|The work area was cordoned off for the whole duration of the visit. The previous preventive visit only involved cleaning the fluid|circuit. The service request was received on 10 March 2026. The customer's head office is in Telford. Access to the machine was|granted after electrical and pneumatic lock-out by the line manager. Adjustments were made with the machine stopped, then|checked in production. Emergency stops were tested and work correctly.|No leak was found on the fittings after repressurisation. No abnormal noise or heating was observed during dry runs.|II. FINDINGS AND READINGS|\n##########doc-005\n||===== PAGE 1 =====|VEXITIK SERVICES LTD|Printed on 5 Apr 2025|sheet 1/4|Report VS-RI-2025-2049|TECHNICAL INTERVENTION REPORT|Report reference : VS-RI-2025-2049|PO number : PO-425523|Job no. : AFF-70040|Customer : Vexdal Pharma, Head office: Swindon|Location : Livingston Works|Installation : Line 1, automatic pipette|Manufacturer : Corovane|Serial number : plate missing|Asset no. : INV-72945|Request date : 14 Mar 2025|Issue date : 24 Mar 2025|Date of intervention : n/a|Machine noise level in operation remained as usual. Suction filters were removed, rinsed and refitted. Frame fixings and hoses|were visually inspected; no corrosion was found.|I. BACKGROUND|Background and equipment|The prevention plan was reviewed with the site safety department before work started. No abnormal noise or heating was observed|during dry runs. Dried product residue on the frame was cleaned off. The circuit was purged until a steady flow was obtained. The|visit concerns the automatic pipette Calanquin 160. It is driven by a Varevex motor, type K73-4P. Guide lubrication was topped up|as per the manual. The maintenance history was reviewed in the customer's logbook.|Course of the visit|The electrical cabinet ventilation was dusted and its filter checked. Products dosed on this line are aqueous and of low viscosity; no|hazardous product was in the circuit during the visit. PLC settings were not changed during the visit. Production data from recent|weeks was reviewed with the customer. The service request was received on 14 March 2025. The customer's head office is in|Swindon. Operators reported short stoppages at shift start, with no alarm message.|Demineralised water at room temperature was used for all tests. Cycle counter readings were entered in the machine logbook.|II. FINDINGS AND READINGS|\n##########doc-006\n||===== PAGE 1 =====|Riliovane Services|Rapport n° DI-RI-2026-3776|Imprimé le 1er octobre 2026|Page 1/3|RAPPORT D'INTERVENTION|Maintenance et contrôle métrologique d'un équipement de dosage|Référence du rapport|DI-RI-2026-3776|N° de commande|CDE-115203|N° d'affaire|AFF-82591|Client|Fromageries Rilvane ; Siège : Saumur|Installation|Ligne 2 ; pompe doseuse à membrane|Équipement|—|Constructeur|Vexlix|N° de série|VE/19/3086|N° d'inventaire|INV-34624|Date de la demande|2 septembre 2026|Date d'émission|16 septembre 2026|Date d'intervention|13 septembre 2026|Contexte et équipement concerné|La purge du circuit a été réalisée jusqu'à obtention d'un écoulement régulier. L'intervention porte sur la pompe doseuse à|\n##########doc-008\n||===== PAGE 1 =====|RAPPORT D'INTERVENTION|Maintenance et contrôle métrologique|RÉFÉRENCE DU RAPPORT|VI-RI-2025-3690|ANNULE ET REMPLACE|VI-RI-2025-3677|PAGE|1/5|DATE D'INTERVENTION|—|N° DE COMMANDE|CDE-184108|N° D'AFFAIRE|AFF-25073|DATE DE LA DEMANDE|28/05/2025|DATE D'ÉMISSION|12/06/2025|SITE|Plateforme de Montargis|INSTALLATION|Ligne 3|remplisseuse rotative|CLIENT|Laboratoires Torzor|Siège : Fougères|ÉQUIPEMENT|Saronis 40|CONSTRUCTEUR|N° D'INVENTAIRE|INV-29599|OBJET|\n##########doc-011\n||===== PAGE 1 =====|SERVICE|REPORT|CONTRACTOR|Fennet Technical Services|REPORT REFERENCE|Ref. FT-RI-2025-2154|STATUS|Compliant|Non-compliant|To be reviewed|Sheet 1/4|Printed on May 25, 2025|Visit record|REPORT REFERENCE|FT-RI-2025-2154|SUPERSEDES|FT-RI-2025-1895|PO NUMBER|PO-759427|JOB NO.|AFF-49973|CUSTOMER|Nevmar Pharma, Head office: Carlow|SITE|Hexham Works|INSTALLATION|Line 3, diaphragm metering pump|EQUIPMENT|Vargen 85|SERIAL NUMBER|—|ASSET NO.|\n##########doc-013\n||===== PAGE 1 =====|RAPPORT|D'INTERVENTION|PRESTATAIRE|Mabindor Mesure et Contrôle|N° DE COMPTE RENDU|Réf. MM-RI-2026-9246|Folio 1/4|Imprimé le 31.07.26|Fiche de l'intervention|N° DE COMPTE RENDU|MM-RI-2026-9246|ANNULE ET REMPLACE|MM-RI-2026-9133|N° DE COMMANDE|CDE-189425|N° D'AFFAIRE|AFF-29406|CLIENT|Laboratoires Vardra, Siège :|Lamballe|LIEU D'INTERVENTION|—|INSTALLATION|Ligne 2, doseuse volumétrique à|piston|ÉQUIPEMENT|Nevul