{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_1049e53a-482e-4256-aaba-d2dc694a87a1","role":"user","created":1795129935,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"chatcmpl-tool-97fcfeede77f635a","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"resultType":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n===== PAGE 1 =====\nVEXITIK SERVICES LTD\nPrinted on 28 Mar 2026\nsheet 1/4\nReport VS-RI-2026-6396\nTECHNICAL INTERVENTION REPORT\nReport reference : VS-RI-2026-6396\nSupersedes : VS-RI-2026-6021\nPO number : PO-879116\nJob no. : AFF-86877\nCustomer : Mirlor Foods, Head office: Telford\nInstallation : Line 1, rotary filling machine\nEquipment : Ulvorgen 600\nManufacturer :\nSerial number : FE836339\nAsset no. : INV-98493\nRequest date : 10 Mar 2026\nIssue date : 23 Mar 2026\nDate of intervention : 22 Mar 2026\nThe customer was briefed on the points of attention noted during the visit. Operators reported short stoppages at shift start, with no\nalarm message. Demineralised water at room temperature was used for all tests.\nI. BACKGROUND\nBackground and equipment\nGuide lubrication was topped up as per the manual. Suction filters were removed, rinsed and refitted. The visit concerns the dosing\nequipment of line 1. It is driven by a Vergen motor, type T91-4P. Checks were carried out with calibrated instruments; certificates\nare available to the customer. The night shift was informed of the adjustments made.\nCourse of the visit\nThe work area was cordoned off for the whole duration of the visit. The previous preventive visit only involved cleaning the fluid\ncircuit. The service request was received on 10 March 2026. The customer's head office is in Telford. Access to the machine was\ngranted after electrical and pneumatic lock-out by the line manager. Adjustments were made with the machine stopped, then\nchecked in production. Emergency stops were tested and work correctly.\nNo leak was found on the fittings after repressurisation. No abnormal noise or heating was observed during dry runs.\nII. FINDINGS AND READINGS\nProducts dosed on this line are aqueous and of low viscosity; no hazardous product was in the circuit during the visit. Operators\nreported short stoppages at shift start, with no alarm message.\nTable 1 - Readings\nQuantity\nValue\nUnit\nObservation\nDose volume as found, trial 1 - head 1\n0.2678\nL\nDose volume as found, trial 2 - head 1\n0.2688\nL\nDose volume as found, trial 3 - head 1\n0.2611\nL\nDose volume as found, trial 1 - head 2\n0.2628\nL\nDose volume as found, trial 2 - head 2\n0.2621\nL\nDose volume as found, trial 3 - head 2\n0.2728\nL\nDose volume as found, trial 1 - head 3\n0.2625\nL\n\n\n[IMAGE p1 #1 bbox=(228,100,368,146) texte OCR:]\nVEXITIK | VS | Services | s Ltd\n\n[IMAGE p1 #2 bbox=(62,273,172,309) texte OCR:]\nF | Fengen\n\n\n===== PAGE 2 =====\nVEXITIK SERVICES LTD\nPrinted on 28 Mar 2026\nsheet 2/4\nReport VS-RI-2026-6396\nDose volume as found, trial 2 - head 3\n0.2657\nL\nDose volume as found, trial 3 - head 3\n0.2695\nL\nDose volume as left, trial 1 - head 1\nn/a\nL\nDose volume as left, trial 2 - head 1\nn/a\nL\nDose volume as left, trial 3 - head 1\nn/a\nL\nDose volume as left, trial 1 - head 2\nn/a\nL\nDose volume as left, trial 2 - head 2\nn/a\nL\nDose volume as left, trial 3 - head 2\nn/a\nL\nDose volume as left, trial 1 - head 3\nn/a\nL\nDose volume as left, trial 2 - head 3\nn/a\nL\nDose volume as left, trial 3 - head 3\nn/a\nL\nDose volume mean as left\nn/a\nL\nsee diagram\nFlow rate as left\nn.m.\nmL/min\nOperating pressure as found\n26.11\npsi\nTank capacity\n1000\nL\nOperating pressure as left\n30.46\npsi\nFlow rate as found\n16950\nmL/min\nLine volume\n4090\nml\nProduct temperature\n29.4\n°C\nIII. WORK PERFORMED\nAdjustments and results\nCleaning-in-place instructions were reminded to the production team. Sensor wiring was inspected and connectors tightened. On\narrival the delivered quantity averaged 0.2659 L.\nReplacements\nThe prevention plan was reviewed with the site safety department before work started. The worn level probe was replaced with a\nnew item, reference FE-546-C. Part FE-750-B (spout seal) was inspected and found in good condition. The electrical cabinet\nventilation was dusted and its filter checked. Machine noise level in operation remained as usual. Quick couplings were\ndismantled, cleaned and refitted with a compatible lubricant.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nprecision balance\nVergen\nEQ-20431\n19 Oct 2025\nreference flow meter\nCorovane\nIN-14187\n1 Dec 2025\nRating\nValue\nNominal volume\n0.25 L\nModel range (OEM)\n100 – 1000 mL\nTank capacity\n1000 L\nLine volume\n4090 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 0.0014 L\nMax. flow\n45000 mL/min\nMax. allowable pressure\n4.5 bar\nRelief valve setting\n3.5 bar\nIV. INSTALLATION DIAGRAM\n\n\n[IMAGE p2 #1 bbox=(56,490,231,558) texte OCR:]\nVERGENMOTOR | TYPET91-4P | N°M8950253 | 1.1kW | 2850min-1 | 230/400V | 50Hz | IP55\n\n\n===== PAGE 3 =====\nVEXITIK SERVICES LTD\nPrinted on 28 Mar 2026\nsheet 3/4\nReport VS-RI-2026-6396\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nV. OBSERVATIONS\nAdditional information, tolerance: ± 6.25 mL.\nThe upstream conveyor Nevalor C74 (flow 41000 mL/min, pressure 4.9 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air\nnetwork runs at 7.0 bar.\nReport prepared by Callum Redding.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: 22 Mar 2027.\nField team\nThe equipment runs on two shifts, five days a week, for liquid product packaging. Callum Redding took part in the visit, at the\nrequest of Hannah Mahon. Guards were refitted and their interlocks checked before restart. The technician checked that no air\nbubbles were present in the circuit before each series of measurements. PLC settings were not changed during the visit.\nTechnician's opinion\nA manual-mode test run preceded the return to automatic operation. The maintenance history was reviewed in the customer's\nlogbook. Machine safety labels are legible and complete. The work station was left clean and clear at the end of the visit. At the\nend of the tests, the equipment must not return to production as it stands.\nApproval workflow\nDried product residue on the frame was cleaned off. The manufacturer's documentation was available on site and up to date.\nProduction data from recent weeks was reviewed with the customer. The transparent guard shows minor scratches with no effect\non safety. The report was reviewed on 23 March 2026. Frame fixings and hoses were visually inspected; no corrosion was found.\nThe circuit was purged until a steady flow was obtained. Cycle counter readings were entered in the machine logbook. The\nproduction manager was kept informed at each step of the visit.\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nFE-750-B\nspout seal\ninspected, kept\n313.87 €\nFE-699-E\nhead solenoid valve\nordered (not fitted)\n30.34 €\nFE-919-E\nfilling cannula\nquoted\n303.06 €\n\n\n[IMAGE p3 #1 bbox=(62,68,542,358) texte OCR:]\nTank | Filling heads | Line: 4090 mL | 2 | Capacity:1000 L | Dose volume asleft:0.2584L\n\n\n===== PAGE 4 =====\nVEXITIK SERVICES LTD\nPrinted on 28 Mar 2026\nsheet 4/4\nReport VS-RI-2026-6396\nVI. CONCLUSION\nLead technician : Erin Thornley\nCustomer approval: James Stroud\nValidation date : 27 Mar 2026\n\n\n[IMAGE p4 #2 bbox=(304,120,414,154) texte OCR:]\nSC | >","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"\n\n===== PAGE 1 =====\nVEXITIK SERVICES LTD\nPrinted on 28 Mar 2026\nsheet 1/4\nReport VS-RI-2026-6396\nTECHNICAL INTERVENTION REPORT\nReport reference : VS-RI-2026-6396\nSupersedes : VS-RI-2026-6021\nPO number : PO-879116\nJob no. : AFF-86877\nCustomer : Mirlor Foods, Head office: Telford\nInstallation : Line 1, rotary filling machine\nEquipment : Ulvorgen 600\nManufacturer :\nSerial number : FE836339\nAsset no. : INV-98493\nRequest date : 10 Mar 2026\nIssue date : 23 Mar 2026\nDate o