{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_d5431ae8-3464-4f10-a229-01da8fde9c28","role":"user","created":1795129956,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"chatcmpl-tool-873915aac9cfd8ec","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"resultType":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n===== PAGE 1 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-2154\nSTATUS\nCompliant\nNon-compliant\nTo be reviewed\nSheet 1/4\nPrinted on May 25, 2025\nVisit record\nREPORT REFERENCE\nFT-RI-2025-2154\nSUPERSEDES\nFT-RI-2025-1895\nPO NUMBER\nPO-759427\nJOB NO.\nAFF-49973\nCUSTOMER\nNevmar Pharma, Head office: Carlow\nSITE\nHexham Works\nINSTALLATION\nLine 3, diaphragm metering pump\nEQUIPMENT\nVargen 85\nSERIAL NUMBER\n—\nASSET NO.\nINV-16947\nREQUEST DATE\nMay 3, 2025\nISSUE DATE\nMay 14, 2025\nBackground and equipment\nCycle counter readings were entered in the machine logbook. The\ncustomer was briefed on the points of attention noted during the\nvisit. The visit concerns the dosing equipment of line 3, whose\nplate reads VA-2023-43119. It is driven by a Fengen motor, type\nM97-4P. Guide lubrication was topped up as per the manual.\nCourse of the visit\nThe equipment runs on two shifts, five days a week, for liquid\nproduct packaging. Suction filters were removed, rinsed and\nrefitted. Cleaning-in-place instructions were reminded to the\nproduction team. The service request was received on 3 May\n2025. The customer's head office is in Carlow. The prevention\nplan was reviewed with the site safety department before work\nstarted. Adjustments were made with the machine stopped, then\nchecked in production. Guards were refitted and their interlocks\nchecked before restart.\n\n\n[IMAGE p1 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n\n===== PAGE 2 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-2154\nSheet 2/4\nPrinted on May 25, 2025\nReadings\nDose volume\nFlow rate\nOperating\npressure\nAs found\n5270\n15.6\n4.0\nE1\n—\n·\n·\nE2\n—\n·\n·\nE3\n—\n·\n·\nAs left\n—\n20.28\nn.m.\nTol.\n± 125 µL\nReadings table units: doses in µL, flow in L/h, pressure in bar, temperature in\n°C.\nRating\nValue\nModel range (OEM)\n1 – 20 mL\nTank capacity\n200 L\nLine volume\n201 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 30 µL\nMax. flow\n37.8 L/h\nMax. allowable pressure\n17.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n8.8 bar\nAdjustments and results\nQuick couplings were dismantled, cleaned and refitted with a\ncompatible lubricant. No leak was found on the fittings after\nrepressurisation. On arrival the delivered quantity averaged 5270\nµL. The transparent guard shows minor scratches with no effect\non safety. Machine safety labels are legible and complete.\nReplacements\nThe production manager was kept informed at each step of the\nvisit. Machine noise level in operation remained as usual. Sensor\nwiring was inspected and connectors tightened. Part VA-270-R\n(discharge valve) was inspected and found in good condition.\nProduction data from recent weeks was reviewed with the\ncustomer.\n\n\n[IMAGE p2 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n[IMAGE p2 #2 bbox=(174,162,236,180) texte OCR:]\n18.3\n\n\n===== PAGE 3 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-2154\nSheet 3/4\nPrinted on May 25, 2025\nDiagram\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6\noutlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nprobe thermometer\nCorovane\nET-78989\nJanuary 5, 2025\nreference flow\nmeter\nNeveltik\nIN-63962\nDecember 5, 2024\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nVA-562-K\nhead gasket\nreplaced\n459.95 €\nVA-270-R\ndischarge valve\ninspected, kept\n410.52 €\nVA-858-K\ndiaphragm\nordered (not fitted)\n511.75 €\nVA-545-R\nsuction valve\nquoted\n495.00 €\nField team\nThe work station was left clean and clear at the end of the visit.\nThe technician checked that no air bubbles were present in the\ncircuit before each series of measurements. The work area was\ncordoned off for the whole duration of the visit. Rhys Ashby took\npart in the visit, at the request of Chloe Harlow. A manual-mode\ntest run preceded the return to automatic operation. Emergency\nstops were tested and work correctly. Checks were carried out\nwith calibrated instruments; certificates are available to the\ncustomer.\nTechnician's opinion\nDried product residue on the frame was cleaned off. Access to the\nmachine was granted after electrical and pneumatic lock-out by\nthe line manager. Frame fixings and hoses were visually\ninspected; no corrosion was found. Tests were run until readings\nwere stable. Products dosed on this line are aqueous and of low\nviscosity; no hazardous product was in the circuit during the visit.\nDemineralised water at room temperature was used for all tests.\nThe circuit was purged until a steady flow was obtained.\nApproval workflow\nThe maintenance history was reviewed in the customer's logbook.\nThe night shift was informed of the adjustments made. The report\nwas reviewed on 15 May 2025.\nObservations\nNote, date of intervention: 10 May 2025.\nFor the record, nominal volume: 5000 µL.\nFor the record, manufacturer: Varevex.\nThe upstream conveyor Pyrinnis C57 (flow 39.96 L/h, pressure\n8.0 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network\nruns at 8.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: November 8, 2025.\n\n\n[IMAGE p3 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n[IMAGE p3 #2 bbox=(36,67,328,243) texte OCR:]\nTank | Pump head | Line: 201 mL | 2 | Capacity: 200 L | Dose volume as left:4930 μL\n\n[IMAGE p3 #3 bbox=(36,276,211,344) texte OCR:]\nFENGENMOTOR | TYPEM97-4P | N°M2877973 | 0.75kW | 2850min-1 | 230/400V | 50Hz | IP55\n\n\n===== PAGE 4 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-2154\nSheet 4/4\nPrinted on May 25, 2025\nLead technician : Sarah Pryce\nCustomer approval: Owen Keane\n\n\n[IMAGE p4 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n[IMAGE p4 #2 bbox=(36,60,146,94) texte OCR:]\nS | <S\n\n[IMAGE p4 #3 bbox=(188,54,322,121) texte OCR:]\nAPPROVED | Nevmar | Pharma | 20 May 2025","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"\n\n===== PAGE 1 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-2154\nSTATUS\nCompliant\nNon-compliant\nTo be reviewed\nSheet 1/4\nPrinted on May 25, 2025\nVisit record\nREPORT REFERENCE\nFT-RI-2025-2154\nSUPERSEDES\nFT-RI-2025-1895\nPO NUMBER\nPO-759427\nJOB NO.\nAFF-49973\nCUSTOMER\nNevmar Pharma, Head office: Carlow\nSITE\nHexham Works\nINSTALLATION\nLine 3, diaphragm metering pump\nEQUIPMENT\nVargen 85\nSERIAL NUMBER\n—\nASSET NO.\nINV-16947\nREQUEST DATE\nMay 3, 2025\nISSUE DATE\nMay 14, 2025\nBackground and equipment\nCycle counter readings were entered in the machine logbook. The\ncustomer was briefed on the points of attention noted during the\nvisit. The visit concerns the dosing equipment of line 3, whose\nplate reads VA-2023-43119. It is driven by a Fengen motor, type\nM97-4P. Guide lubrication was topped up as per the manual.\nCourse of the visit\nThe equipment runs on two shifts, five days a week, for liquid\nproduct packaging. Suction filters were removed, rinsed and\nrefitted. Cleaning-in-place instructions were reminded to the\nproduction team. The service request was received on 3 May\n2025. The customer's head office is in Carlow. The prevention\nplan was reviewed with the site safety department before work\nstarted. Adjustments were made with the machine stopped, then\nchecked in production. Guards were refitted and their interlocks\nchecked before restart.\n\n\n[IMAGE p1 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n\n===== PAGE 2 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-2154\nSheet 2/4\nPrinted on May 25, 2025\nReadings\nDose volume\nFlow rate\nOperating\npressure\nAs found\n5270\n15.6\n4.0\nE1\n—\n·\n·\nE2\n—\n·\n·\nE3\n—\n·\n·\nAs left\n—\n20.28\nn.m.\nTol.\n± 125 µL\nReadings table units: doses in µL, flow in L/h, pressure in bar, temperature in\n°C.\nRating\nValue\nModel range (OEM)\n1 – 20 mL\nTank capacity\n200 L\nLine volume\n201 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 30 µL\nMax. flow\n37.8 L/h\nMax. allowable pressure\n17.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n8.8 bar\nAdjustments and results\nQuick couplings were dismantled, cleaned and refitted with a\ncompatible lubricant. No leak was found on the fittings after\nrepressurisation. On arrival the delivered quantity averaged 5270\nµL. The transparent guard shows minor scratches with no effect\non safety. Machine safety labels are legible and complete.\nReplacements\nThe production manager was kept informed at each step of the\nvisit. Machine noise level in operation remained as usual. Sensor\nwiring was inspected and connectors tightened. Part VA-270-R\n(discharge valve) was inspected and found in good condition.\nProduction data from recent weeks was reviewed with the\ncustomer.\n\n\n[IMAGE p2 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n[IMAGE p2 #2 bbox=(174,162,236,180) texte OCR:]\n18.3\n\n\n===== PAGE 3 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-2154\nSheet 3/4\nPrinted on May 25, 2025\nDiagram\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6\noutlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nprobe thermometer\nCorovane\nET-78989\nJanuary 5, 2025\nreference flow\nmeter\nNeveltik\nIN-63962\nDecember 5, 2024\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nVA-562-K\nhead gasket\nreplaced\n459.95 €\nVA-270-R\ndischarge valve\ninspected, kept\n410.52 €\nVA-858-K\ndiaphragm\nordered (not fitted)\n511.75 €\nVA-545-R\nsuction valve\nquoted\n495.00 €\nField team\nThe work station was left clean and clear at the end of the visit.\nThe technician checked that no air bubbles were present in the\ncircuit before each series of measurements. The work area was\ncordoned off for the whole duration of the visit. Rhys Ashby took\npart in the visit, at the request of Chloe Harlow. A manual-mode\ntest run preceded the return to automatic operation. Emergency\nstops were tested and work correctly. Checks were carried out\nwith calibrated instruments; certificates are available to the\ncustomer.\nTechnician's opinion\nDried product residue on the frame was cleaned off. Access to the\nmachine was granted after electrical and pneumatic lock-out by\nthe line manager. Frame fixings and hoses were visually\ninspected; no corrosion was found. Tests were run until readings\nwere stable. Products dosed on this line are aqueous and of low\nviscosity; no hazardous product was in the circuit during the visit.\nDemineralised water at room temperature was used for all tests.\nThe circuit was purged until a steady flow was obtained.\nApproval workflow\nThe maintenance history was reviewed in the customer's logbook.\nThe night shift was informed of the adjustments made. The report\nwas reviewed on 15 May 2025.\nObservations\nNote, date of intervention: 10 May 2025.\nFor the record, nominal volume: 5000 µL.\nFor the record, manufacturer: Varevex.\nThe upstream conveyor Pyrinnis C57 (flow 39.96 L/h, pressure\n8.0 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network\nruns at 8.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: November 8, 2025.\n\n\n[IMAGE p3 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n[IMAGE p3 #2 bbox=(36,67,328,243) texte OCR:]\nTank | Pump head | Line: 201 mL | 2 | Capacity: 200 L | Dose volume as left:4930 μL\n\n[IMAGE p3 #3 bbox=(36,276,211,344) texte OCR:]\nFENGENMOTOR | TYPEM97-4P | N°M2877973 | 0.75kW | 2850min-1 | 230/400V | 50Hz | IP55\n\n\n===== PAGE 4 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-2154\nSheet 4/4\nPrinted on May 25, 2025\nLead technician : Sarah Pryce\nCustomer approval: Owen Keane\n\n\n[IMAGE p4 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n[IMAGE p4 #2 bbox=(36,60,146,94) texte OCR:]\nS | <S\n\n[IMAGE p4 #3 bbox=(188,54,322,121) texte OCR:]\nAPPROVED | Nevmar | Pharma | 20 May 2025","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
