{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1795130019-ZRX19wjTg8PuhBDr8Dde","role":"assistant","created":1795130024,"content":[{"type":"toolRequest","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1776b2af84896ce","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cd /travail && cat work/textes/doc-052.txt; echo \"#################### 060\"; cat work/textes/doc-060.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose.toolCall.providerIndex":0,"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true,"inference":{"provider":"openai","requestedModel":"deepseek-v4.1-flash"},"operations":{"llm":{"advertised_tools":["analyze","apps__create_app","apps__delete_app","apps__iterate_app","apps__list_apps","delegate","edit","extensionmanager__list_resources","extensionmanager__manage_extensions","extensionmanager__read_resource","extensionmanager__search_available_extensions","load","load_skill","read_image","shell","tree","write"]}}}}}
{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_39145613-aa4d-4f2b-9fe7-31421a03163c","role":"user","created":1795130024,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1776b2af84896ce","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"resultType":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n===== PAGE 1 =====\nNEVEVEX CALIBRATION LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. NC-RI-2026-6182\nPrinted on 30/08/2026\n1 / 3\nSERVICE REPORT\nInspection and maintenance\nDocument no. :\nNC-RI-2026-6182\nPO number :\nPO-632511\nJob no. :\nAFF-22331\nCustomer :\nTordra Pharma, Head office: Kendal\nInstallation :\nLine 3, piston filler\nEquipment :\nCorvex 120\nBrand :\nNevvex\nS/N :\nNE321197\nAsset no. :\nINV-11868\nRequest date :\n07/08/2026\nIssue date :\n16/08/2026\nDate of intervention :\n12/08/2026\nBackground and equipment\nDemineralised water at room temperature was used for all tests. The visit concerns the dosing equipment of line 3. It is driven by\na Pradal motor, type M89-2P. Emergency stops were tested and work correctly.\nCourse of the visit\nThe transparent guard shows minor scratches with no effect on safety. The service request was received on 7 August 2026. The\ncustomer's head office is in Kendal.\nReadings\nParameter\nValue\nDose volume, as found, E1-E3\n5.32 ; 5.31 ; 5.36\nDose volume, as left, E1-E3\n— ; — ; —\nDose volume, mean as left\n—\nDelivery rate, as found\n3'440\nDelivery rate, as left\n—\nOperating pressure, as found\n1.6\nOperating pressure, as left\n—\nProduct temperature (°C)\n31.6\nRating\nValue\nNominal volume\n5 cm³\nModel range (OEM)\n5 – 500 mL\nTank capacity\n50 L\nLine volume\n537 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 0.04 mL\nMax. flow\n9'500 mL/min\nMax. allowable pressure\n4.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n2.7 bar\nAdjustments and results\nThe customer was briefed on the points of attention noted during the visit. After several stroke adjustments, the delivered quantity\nsettled at 5.07 mL on average, against 5.33 mL on arrival. Production data from recent weeks was reviewed with the customer.\nReplacements\nDried product residue on the frame was cleaned off. No replacement was needed; part NE-119-C (check valve) was nevertheless\nordered as a precaution. Part NE-761-A (dosing nozzle) was inspected and found in good condition. Operators reported short\nstoppages at shift start, with no alarm message.\nDiagram\n\n\n[IMAGE p1 #1 bbox=(437,59,557,98) texte OCR:]\nNEVEVEX | NC | Calibration Ltd\n\n\n===== PAGE 2 =====\nNEVEVEX CALIBRATION LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. NC-RI-2026-6182\nPrinted on 30/08/2026\n2 / 3\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nreference pressure\ngauge\nCorovane\nET-17479\n26/02/2026\nprecision balance\nVarevex\nIN-56349\n01/07/2026\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nNE-761-A\ndosing nozzle\ninspected, kept\n591.38 €\nNE-119-C\ncheck valve\nordered (not fitted)\n92.28 €\nNE-721-E\nreturn spring\nquoted\n90.48 €\nNo part was replaced during this visit.\nField team\nProducts dosed on this line are aqueous and of low viscosity; no hazardous product was in the circuit during the visit. Megan\nThornley took part in the visit, at the request of James Gallagher.\nTechnician's opinion\nChecks were carried out with calibrated instruments; certificates are available to the customer. At the end of the tests, the\nequipment may return to production without restriction. The circuit was purged until a steady flow was obtained.\nApproval workflow\nThe work area was cordoned off for the whole duration of the visit. The report was reviewed on 17 August 2026.\nNotes\nAdditional information, delivery rate as left: 3'730 mL/min.\nAdditional information, operating pressure as left: 1.8 bar.\nThe upstream conveyor Riliovane C27 (flow 5'770 mL/min, pressure 3.3 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air\nnetwork runs at 7.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: 12/08/2027.\n\n\n[IMAGE p2 #1 bbox=(40,56,462,311) texte OCR:]\nTank | Piston unit | Line: 537 mL | 2 | Capacity: 50 L\n\n[IMAGE p2 #2 bbox=(34,335,209,403) texte OCR:]\nPRADALMOTOR | TYPEM89-2P | N°M5449010 | 1.5kW | 1380min-1 | 400V | 50Hz | IP55\n\n\n===== PAGE 3 =====\n\n\n[IMAGE p3 #1 bbox=(0,0,595,842) texte OCR:]\nNEVEVEXCALIBRATIONLTD |SERVICEREPORT | Ref.NC-RI-2026-6182 | Lead technician:SarahStroud | Customer approval:Rhys Doyle | Validationdate: | Printedon30/08/2026 | 3/3#################### 060\n\n\n===== PAGE 1 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-5506\nSTATUS\nCompliant\nNon-compliant\nTo be reviewed\nSheet 1/3\nPrinted on November 30, 2025\nVisit record\nREPORT REFERENCE\nFT-RI-2025-5506\nPO NUMBER\nPO-712867\nJOB NO.\nAFF-25491\nCUSTOMER\nDravex Beverages, Head office:\nWrexham\nPLANT\nAthlone Facility\nINSTALLATION\nLine 2, automatic pipette\nEQUIPMENT\n—\nBRAND\nOstiovan\nSERIAL NUMBER\nplate missing\nASSET NO.\nINV-35104\nREQUEST DATE\nNovember 2, 2025\nISSUE DATE\nNovember 16, 2025\nBackground and equipment\nThe manufacturer's documentation was available on site and up\nto date. Guards were refitted and their interlocks checked before\nrestart. The circuit was purged until a steady flow was obtained.\nThe visit concerns the dosing equipment of line 2. It is driven by a\nCorovane motor, type K67-2P.\nCourse of the visit\nThe prevention plan was reviewed with the site safety department\nbefore work started. The service request was received on 2\nNovember 2025. The customer's head office is in Wrexham.\nMachine noise level in operation remained as usual. The\ncustomer was briefed on the points of attention noted during the\nvisit.\n\n\n[IMAGE p1 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n\n===== PAGE 2 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-5506\nSheet 2/3\nPrinted on November 30, 2025\nReadings\nDose\nThroughput\nOperating\npressure\nAs found\n0.568\n6\n0.6\nE1\n0.536\n·\n·\nE2\n0.552\n·\n·\nE3\n0.526\n·\n·\nAs left\n0.538\n7\n—\nTol.\nReadings table units: doses in mL, flow in mL/min, pressure in bar,\ntemperature in °C.\nRating\nValue\nModel range (OEM)\n0.5 – 5 mL\nTank capacity\n0.25 L\nLine volume\n18 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 0.022 mL\nMax. flow\n20 mL/min\nMax. allowable pressure\n2.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n0.9 bar\nStep\nDate\nIncident reported\nOctober 31, 2025\nService request\nNovember 2, 2025\nService date\nNovember 11, 2025\nReport issued\nNovember 16, 2025\nAdjustments and results\nThe technician checked that no air bubbles were present in the\ncircuit before each series of measurements. The equipment runs\non two shifts, five days a week, for liquid product packaging. PLC\nsettings were not changed during the visit. On arrival the delivered\nquantity averaged 0.568 mL. The deviation allowed by the\ncustomer's specification is ± 0.075 mL. Pressure settled at 0.7\nbar, the relief valve remaining set at 0.9 bar. The work station was\nleft clean and clear at the end of the visit. Quick couplings were\ndismantled, cleaned and refitted with a compatible lubricant.\nReplacements\nOperators reported short stoppages at shift start, with no alarm\nmessage. No replacement was needed; part OS-706-C\n(aspiration filter) was nevertheless ordered as a precaution. Part\nOS-719-D (piston O-ring) was inspected and found in good\ncondition. Dried product residue on the frame was cleaned off. No\nleak was found on the fittings after repressurisation.\n\n\n[IMAGE p2 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n\n===== PAGE 3 =====\nSERVICE\nREPORT\nCONTRACTOR\nFennet Technical Services\nREPORT REFERENCE\nRef. FT-RI-2025-5506\nSheet 3/3\nPrinted on November 30, 2025\nDiagram\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6\noutlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nreference flow\nmeter\nNeveltik\nEQ-87611\nApril 18, 2025\nprobe thermometer\nFenpax\nET-26836\nSeptember 5, 2025\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nOS-719-D\npiston O-ring\ninspected, kept\n287.18 €\nOS-706-C\naspiration filter\nordered (not fitted)\n439.66 €\nOS-784-D\ntip ejector\nquoted\n185.32 €\nNo part was replaced during this visit.\nField team\nFrame fixings and hoses were visually inspected; no corrosion\nwas found. Machine safety labels are legible and complete. Chloe\nRedding led the visit with the support of Erin Harlow, at the\nrequest of Megan Keane.\nTechnician's opinion\nAdjustments were made with the machine stopped, then checked\nin production. Tests were run until readings were stable. Checks\nwere carried out with calibrated instruments; certificates are\navailable to the customer. A manual-mode test run preceded the\nreturn to automatic operation.\nApproval workflow\nProduction data from recent weeks was reviewed with the\ncustomer. The report was reviewed on 19 November 2025. The\nnight shift was informed of the adjustments made. Emergency\nstops were tested and work correctly.\nObservations\nNote, equipment: Kaltis 40.\nThe upstream conveyor Nevalor C52 (flow 13 mL/min, pressure\n1.5 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network\nruns at 7.0 bar.\nReport prepared by Erin Harlow.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: May 12, 2026.\nTechnician:\nCustomer approval: Aoife Calloway\nApproval date : November 23, 2025\n\n\n[IMAGE p3 #1 bbox=(662,43,800,88) texte OCR:]\nFENNET | FT | Technical Services\n\n[IMAGE p3 #2 bbox=(36,67,328,243) texte OCR:]\nTank | Pipetting module | Line: 18 mL | 2 | Set point: 0.5 mL | Capacity: 0.25 L\n\n[IMAGE p3 #3 bbox=(36,276,211,344) texte OCR:]\nCOROVANEMOTOR | TYPEK67-2P | N°M5716919 | 0.75kW | 2850min-1 | 400V | 50Hz | IP55\n\n[IMAGE p3 #4 bbox=(348,433,458,467) texte OCR:]\n2","annotations":{"pri