{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1795130680-2JJP3QWlRCqrtFprm4zL","role":"assistant","created":1795130683,"content":[{"type":"toolRequest","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5f59e4b23a60fce","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cd /travail && sed -n 190,215p work/textes/doc-060.txt && echo ====036 && sed -n 185,215p work/textes/doc-036.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose.toolCall.providerIndex":0,"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true,"inference":{"provider":"openai","requestedModel":"deepseek-v4.1-flash"},"operations":{"llm":{"advertised_tools":["analyze","apps__create_app","apps__delete_app","apps__iterate_app","apps__list_apps","delegate","edit","extensionmanager__list_resources","extensionmanager__manage_extensions","extensionmanager__read_resource","extensionmanager__search_available_extensions","load","load_skill","read_image","shell","tree","write"]}}}}}
{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_1d232911-9c31-4ac7-bbd9-bc8cb789da96","role":"user","created":1795130683,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5f59e4b23a60fce","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"resultType":"complete","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No part was replaced during this visit.\nField team\nFrame fixings and hoses were visually inspected; no corrosion\nwas found. Machine safety labels are legible and complete. Chloe\nRedding led the visit with the support of Erin Harlow, at the\nrequest of Megan Keane.\nTechnician's opinion\nAdjustments were made with the machine stopped, then checked\nin production. Tests were run until readings were stable. Checks\nwere carried out with calibrated instruments; certificates are\navailable to the customer. A manual-mode test run preceded the\nreturn to automatic operation.\nApproval workflow\nProduction data from recent weeks was reviewed with the\ncustomer. The report was reviewed on 19 November 2025. The\nnight shift was informed of the adjustments made. Emergency\nstops were tested and work correctly.\nObservations\nNote, equipment: Kaltis 40.\nThe upstream conveyor Nevalor C52 (flow 13 mL/min, pressure\n1.5 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network\nruns at 7.0 bar.\nReport prepared by Erin Harlow.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: May 12, 2026.\nTechnician:\n====036\naspiration filter\nquoted\n551.28 €\nField team\nThe electrical cabinet ventilation was dusted and its filter checked.\nThe maintenance history was reviewed in the customer's logbook.\nNo abnormal noise or heating was observed during dry runs.\nEthan Pryce took part in the visit, at the request of Chloe Doyle.\nThe previous preventive visit only involved cleaning the fluid\ncircuit.\nTechnician's opinion\nThe technician checked that no air bubbles were present in the\ncircuit before each series of measurements. Guards were refitted\nand their interlocks checked before restart. Tests were run until\nreadings were stable. The work station was left clean and clear at\nthe end of the visit. Suction filters were removed, rinsed and\nrefitted.\nApproval workflow\nThe production manager was kept informed at each step of the\nvisit. Dried product residue on the frame was cleaned off.\nReviewed on 26 April 2026, the report was approved by Olivia\nGallagher on 30 April 2026. Machine safety labels are legible and\ncomplete.\nObservations\nFor the record, operating pressure as left: 0.6 bar.\nThe upstream conveyor Nevalor C76 (flow 35 mL/min, pressure\n2.7 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network\nruns at 6.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: October 20, 2026.\n","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"No part was replaced during this visit.\nField team\nFrame fixings and hoses were visually inspected; no corrosion\nwas found. Machine safety labels are legible and complete. Chloe\nRedding led the visit with the support of Erin Harlow, at the\nrequest of Megan Keane.\nTechnician's opinion\nAdjustments were made with the machine stopped, then checked\nin production. Tests were run until readings were stable. Checks\nwere carried out with calibrated instruments; certificates are\navailable to the customer. A manual-mode test run preceded the\nreturn to automatic operation.\nApproval workflow\nProduction data from recent weeks was reviewed with the\ncustomer. The report was reviewed on 19 November 2025. The\nnight shift was informed of the adjustments made. Emergency\nstops were tested and work correctly.\nObservations\nNote, equipment: Kaltis 40.\nThe upstream conveyor Nevalor C52 (flow 13 mL/min, pressure\n1.5 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network\nruns at 7.0 bar.\nReport prepared by Erin Harlow.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: May 12, 2026.\nTechnician:\n====036\naspiration filter\nquoted\n551.28 €\nField team\nThe electrical cabinet ventilation was dusted and its filter checked.\nThe maintenance history was reviewed in the customer's logbook.\nNo abnormal noise or heating was observed during dry runs.\nEthan Pryce took part in the visit, at the request of Chloe Doyle.\nThe previous preventive visit only involved cleaning the fluid\ncircuit.\nTechnician's opinion\nThe technician checked that no air bubbles were present in the\ncircuit before each series of measurements. Guards were refitted\nand their interlocks checked before restart. Tests were run until\nreadings were stable. The work station was left clean and clear at\nthe end of the visit. Suction filters were removed, rinsed and\nrefitted.\nApproval workflow\nThe production manager was kept informed at each step of the\nvisit. Dried product residue on the frame was cleaned off.\nReviewed on 26 April 2026, the report was approved by Olivia\nGallagher on 30 April 2026. Machine safety labels are legible and\ncomplete.\nObservations\nFor the record, operating pressure as left: 0.6 bar.\nThe upstream conveyor Nevalor C76 (flow 35 mL/min, pressure\n2.7 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network\nruns at 6.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: October 20, 2026.\n","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
